KG42.register("rules-2c86a1553633354c3544af7d",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R009","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"The energy offered for sharing in the local P2P market is participants' surplus renewable energy, with solar photovoltaics and wind turbines given as generation examples. Scope: The proposed P2P market whose participants are connected to the local distribution network.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"The proposed P2P market whose participants are connected to the local distribution network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E05"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The energy offered for sharing in the local P2P market is participants' surplus renewable energy, with solar photovoltaics and wind turbines given as generation examples. Scope: The proposed P2P market whose participants are connected to the local distribution network.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E05"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2 System configuration","anchor_text":"b­ nt The remainder of the paper is organized as follows. Section 2 in­ troduces a representative sy","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The most representative structure of the peer-to-peer energy trading market with shared energy storage units is shown in Fig. 1. In such a P2P market, a participant who has excessive energy and sells energy to other participants or the power grid is defined as a typical energy seller, e.g., a rooftop PV plant. A participant who consumes energy and buys energy from energy sellers or power grid is identified as a typical energy buyer, e.g., a community. Energy sellers and buyers in the P2P market can trade with each other freely and reach a bilaterally satisfactory transaction result. The solid arrows present the P2P transaction between typical energy sellers and energy buyers. All participants are connected with the local distribution network and the energy trading can be finished through physical power transmission lines."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1 Energy sellers","anchor_text":"B. Zheng et al. In summary, the whole P2P market is composed of three types of en stakeholders: ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In summary, the whole P2P market is composed of three types of stakeholders: energy sellers, energy buyers, and an aggregator. The detailed introduction of each stakeholder is presented as follows: Energy sellers consist of participants with renewable power generation, e.g., solar photovoltaics, wind turbine. These participants have surplus renewable energy and would like to share energy with other people in the P2P market to get a financial payoff. They can also choose to sell energy to the power grid in a traditional FiT scheme. Each energy seller, whose goal is to maximize personal profit, decides to participate in the P2P transaction market or trade with power utility according to the price signal. Energy sellers’ renewable energy supply is intermittent and volatile. However, to facilitate our P2P transaction, we assume each energy seller has been equipped with a storage device or other power electronic device to stabilize their energy supply in a certain time slot."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No decision variable is defined within this rule's scope. The source identifies the product qualitatively as surplus renewable energy and gives PV/wind examples; it does not define a local-product design selection or operational decision here.","empty_theta_reason":"No parameter is quantified for product.local_energy itself. The supplied evidence gives no numeric coefficient, capacity, unit, or domain specific to the local energy product; symbols such as P_s^t belong to the seller clearing problem rather than this qualitative product definition."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","quote":"Energy sellers consist of participants with renewable power generation, e.g., solar photovoltaics, wind turbine. These participants have surplus renewable energy and would like to share energy with other people in the P2P market to get a financial payoff."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","quote":"All participants are connected with the local distribution network and the energy trading can be finished through physical power transmission lines."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"66aebc3d5e2f2a18a241ddd85394495b4325cba1e24182aaa85bb9d62e176d5c","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied source evidence defines the local energy product qualitatively: energy sellers have surplus renewable generation, with solar photovoltaics and wind turbines as examples, and participants are connected to the local distribution network. The rule contains no equation, quantitative variable, parameter value, unit, or domain specific to product.local_energy. The seller-side quantity P_s^t and transaction amount p_sb^t are defined in the seller clearing problem, not as a mathematical definition of this product rule. B evidence remains unreviewed; this assessment is based on the supplied quotations and does not claim independent source verification.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The qualitative product-scope constraint is owned by the local-energy-product node; this frozen rule contains no edge for the product relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
